# Gladia Skills Conventions

## SDK-First Policy

All code examples MUST use the official Gladia SDK (`@gladiaio/sdk` for JS/TS, `gladiaio-sdk` for Python). Only use raw REST/WebSocket as a documented fallback when the SDK cannot satisfy the requirement or the user explicitly requests direct protocol-level control.

## Skill Structure

- Each skill lives in `plugins/gladia/skills/<skill-name>/`
- `SKILL.md` is required; move detailed content to `references/` subdirectory
- Keep SKILL.md under ~300 lines / ~800 words
- Reference files over 100 lines need a `## Contents` table of contents
- Cross-reference `gladia-sdk-integration` and `gladia-troubleshooting` from every use-case skill

## Code Generation

- Assume `GladiaClient` is already initialized — do not show init code in use-case skills
- Point to `sdk-integration` skill for setup and initialization
- Include examples in both JavaScript/TypeScript and Python
- Do not hardcode SDK versions — they are CI-managed in `sdk-versions.md`

## CI-Managed Files (do not edit)

- `plugins/gladia/skills/gladia-documentation-auto/SKILL.md` — synced from docs.gladia.io
- `plugins/gladia/skills/gladia-sdk-integration/references/sdk-versions.md` — synced from npm/PyPI
